# Production incident (2026-09-18) — history, so nobody re-adds a redirect rule here without
# reading this first. The same-origin auth proxy (Safari third-party-cookie fix; see
# netlify/edge-functions/auth-proxy.mjs) went through three attempts:
#   1. netlify.toml [[redirects]] with an (invalid) `context = "..."` field — silently
#      discarded entirely, total login outage on every browser.
#   2. The two rules moved to THIS file, ahead of the catch-all below (this file is processed
#      before netlify.toml, which is why attempt 1's rules never had a chance either way) —
#      fixed the 404s, but Netlify's declarative redirect/rewrite engine does not reliably
#      relay Set-Cookie headers back to the client, so refresh_token/CSRF cookies still never
#      reached the browser. Confirmed against Netlify's own support forum/docs.
#   3. netlify/edge-functions/auth-proxy.mjs — full programmatic control over the Response,
#      including Headers.getSetCookie() to relay cookies correctly. This is the one that
#      actually works, and it runs BEFORE this file's rules are even considered (Edge
#      Functions execute first in Netlify's request chain), so it does not need a rule here.
#
# Original rule — SPA fallback. Load-bearing since hash-based routing was removed (see
# ARD-Wohnungsmieten.md ADR-001): every in-app route (/properties/:id, /auth/verify-email, …) is
# now a real path the server receives directly, so EVERY one of them depends on this rule to get
# the app shell instead of a raw 404 — not just a stray non-hash URL anymore.
/*    /index.html   200
